<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n11316" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">corruptĭo</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">conr-</span></b> ),
		ōnis, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>f</i> [corrumpo]. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>Act., a corrupting, spoiling, seducing</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">militum,</span>”
				<i>bribery</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Tac. A.
					11, 2</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">judicii,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ascon. ad Cic. Verr. 1, 6, 15, p.
				131</span></i>
			 Bait. —<b>
				<i>Absol.</i>
			</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">eo usque corruptionis provectus est, ut, etc.,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Tac. A.
					2, 55</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>Pass., a corrupt condition, corruption</i> (very
			rare): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">totius corporis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Tusc. 4, 13, 29</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">opinionum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Tusc. 4, 13, 29</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
